<!-- SEOAI:QACONTENT:START --><script type="application/ld+json">{"@type":"FAQPage","@context":"https://schema.org","mainEntity":[{"name":"How does AI customer support affect customer satisfaction?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"Done right, AI improves satisfaction by eliminating wait times and providing instant, accurate responses. Our implementations average 4.8/5 CSAT scores—higher than human-only support. The key is building AI that knows its limits and escalates gracefully when needed.","@type":"Answer"}},{"name":"What percentage of support tickets can AI actually resolve?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"Typically 60-80% of tier-1 tickets are automatable: password resets, order status, billing questions, return requests, and basic troubleshooting. Complex technical issues, emotional situations, and edge cases still need human agents—but AI can assist them too.","@type":"Answer"}},{"name":"How long does it take to train AI on our products and policies?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"Initial training takes 2-3 weeks using your existing documentation, help articles, and ticket history. The AI continues learning from every interaction, so accuracy improves over time. Most clients see 85%+ accuracy within the first month of deployment.","@type":"Answer"}},{"name":"Will AI replace our support team?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"AI handles volume so your team can focus on complex issues, relationship building, and high-value interactions. Most clients don't reduce headcount—they handle 3-5x more volume with the same team while improving response quality and employee satisfaction.","@type":"Answer"}},{"name":"How do you handle sensitive customer data?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"We deploy within your existing security perimeter. Data stays in your environment, models can run on-premise or in your cloud, and we support SOC 2, HIPAA, and GDPR compliance. AI never trains on customer data without